@startuml soil_classes
title Soil (tp::soil): from what a track is made of to how it behaves
hide empty members
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "tp::math (see core_classes)" {
  class "exp(x)" as Exp <<free function>>
}

package "tp::soil" {
  class Composition <<struct>> {
    +clay_fraction : double, 0 sand .. 1 clay
    +moisture : double, kg water / kg dry soil
    +compaction : double, 0 loose .. 1 rolled
  }
  class Surface <<struct>> {
    +cone_index_pa : double
    +grip_factor : double
    +spin_fall_off : double
  }
  enum ParamError {
    kNotFinite
    kClayFractionOutOfRange
    kMoistureOutOfRange
    kCompactionOutOfRange
  }
  class "soil functions" as SoilFns <<free functions>> {
    +{static} kMaxMoisture = 0.5
    +validate(const Composition&) : optional<ParamError>
    +surface(const Composition&) : Surface
  }
  SoilFns ..> Composition
  SoilFns ..> Surface
  SoilFns ..> ParamError
}
SoilFns ..> Exp
note bottom of SoilFns
  strength: sand peaks near 8 % moisture, clay weakens as it gets wetter;
  compaction raises both; mixed by clay fraction
  grip: dust on dry clay, a slick film above clay's plastic limit
  fall-off: base + sand digging + wet clay smearing
end note
@enduml
